I've written the session plan: two task files and an issue-responses file in session_plan/. The commit didn't go through because session_plan/ is in .gitignore. The harness's || true lets that pass, and the files are on disk.

Task 1 (product): `/run` hangs when a background job keeps the output open.
• The bug: yoyo run 'sleep 6 & echo hi' takes the full 6 seconds, because run_shell_command reads output to the end before waiting for the shell. A command like python3 -m http.server & would block until the server dies.
• The fix: copy what the model's bash tool already does (src/tools.rs, the #1049 fix): wait for the shell to exit, then give the output reader 2 more seconds. The task asks for a commit-body list of every difference from that version, not just the ones chosen.
• Tests: written first. The background case must return under about 3.5s. Plain commands, exit codes, and output written before the shell exits must stay exactly as today.
• Also in the task: check /bg and /watch for the same problem and file an issue rather than fixing them, since the task is capped at 3 files.

Task 2 (product, Part of #1009): shell `outline` and `watch` get literal quotes around a spaced argument.
• Probe: I re-ran all eight still-open verbs on today's binary (run and map were already fixed and marked so on the ticket) and posted the table on #1009.
  • find, blame and grep now work.
  • outline and watch still do harm. outline reports a false "no symbols" with exit 0, and watch saves "echo a b" as a single quoted word.
  • docs, lint and skill only show the quotes inside an error message, so they stay on the ticket.
• The fix: reuse the argument handling from the earlier run and map fixes; the task says not to write a third mechanism.

